    "updated_at": "2022-06-16T07:10:19Z",
    "body": "See the discussion in https://github.com/w3c/FileAPI/issues/47. @saschanaz has been doing some work in this area and it seems rather hard to completely prevent a `File` object from being readable after its backing file was modified on disk. For typical cases where the backing file's timestamp changes we can do it, but if that stays the change there's not really a way to do it.",
